  "goodToKnow": "Das Heizöl is heating oil. Around a quarter of German homes still heat with oil, usually from a tank in the cellar filled by a tanker truck. Under the 2024 Gebäudeenergiegesetz, newly installed heating systems must eventually use 65 percent renewable energy, promoting Wärmepumpen (heat pumps) over new oil boilers. Heizen means to heat. It has no plural."
